# Wave W17-Y (Lake Gallant): light post — a shore-light post at the lake’s rim: a straight post carrying a warm lamp head, one of the kind shore lights the design rings the water with, standing here at the lake’s north corners where the road meets the shore (design: the embankment and shore lights ring the water). On gallant turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the shipped lanternpost dressing kind by register entire (the plan’s own split: these are the lake’s own lights, placed by this kit) and from the fleet’s marker posts by the lamp: posts mark, this light keeps the shore.
